tact community (TODO: reference the issue) \n- part of `duecredit` collection\n- if provides some additional service as \n  - report new version(s) available\n  - list which other software might be of interest\n\nCollections methodologies (should be configurable per project although @yarikoptic likes cached one big one instead of many small ones):\n- immediate upon invocation\n- cached collection which would then get submitted only after some time has passed since last submission or on cron, etc\n\nWhat to collect\n- UUID  (zenodo???)\n- name of the package/software\n  - possibly with indication that it was triggered by some other package on top (e.g. fmriprep calling out to nipype and then freesurfer etc)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"b6514b9b57c47fbb79fc9d0864ed8b5f63682d4e"},"timestamp":1549307228,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDM2MDEzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2906#issuecomment-460360133"},"message":"API on the server side:\n\n- GET /version/{project}\n- GET /ping\n- POST /ping","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"b6514b9b57c47fbb79fc9d0864ed8b5f63682d4e"},"timestamp":1549307228,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDAxNjM2NA=="},"target":"5f29b5548b544a6a4bcd069e432093ea8acbccffa04546feb36feeeb935ec7d9","message":"API on the server side:\n\n- GET /version/{project}\n- GET /ping\n- POST /ping (for submitting JSON records)\n\nwe should use: https://aiohttp.readthedocs.io/en/stable/index.html","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"b6514b9b57c47fbb79fc9d0864ed8b5f63682d4e"},"timestamp":1549307459,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDAxNzg5OQ=="},"target":"5f29b5548b544a6a4bcd069e432093ea8acbccffa04546feb36feeeb935ec7d9","message":"API on the server side:\n\n- GET /version/{project}\n- GET /ping\n- POST /ping (for submitting JSON records)\n\nwe should use: https://aiohttp.readthedocs.io/en/stable/index.html\n\nor possibly: https://transmute-core.readthedocs.io/en/latest/","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"b6514b9b57c47fbb79fc9d0864ed8b5f63682d4e"},"timestamp":1549307510,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE4MDAxODIyNQ=="},"target":"5f29b5548b544a6a4bcd069e432093ea8acbccffa04546feb36feeeb935ec7d9","message":"API on the server side:\n\n- GET /version/{project}\n- GET /ping\n- POST /ping (for submitting JSON records)\n\nwe should use: https://aiohttp.readthedocs.io/en/stable/index.html\n\nor possibly: https://transmute-core.readthedocs.io/en/latest/\n\nhttps://aiohttp-transmute.readthedocs.io/en/latest/","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cb97d7dcb4c97450b1037073d98f8fe23d8199e5"},"timestamp":1549342731,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MDUxMzM4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2906#issuecomment-460513388"},"message":"Thanks for pinging me! Here is a summary of our experiences with popylar: \n\nAs far as we can tell, the technical solution works well. The main challenges are social. Using Google Analytics as the data collection mechanism is probably a non-starter, because many users would consider the merge of their already collected data about browser/mail and so on, together with software usage patterns to be unacceptable. And I think that it wouldn't be a stretch. \n\nUsers may have concerns even in the absence of the specific concerns related to GA. Opt-in seems to be the way to go, but likely to reduce your sample, and introduce biases. \n\nFor Popylar in particular, I am wary of \"heavy\" solutions that require setting up persistent infrastructure (such as a database), because I think that this would raise a high barrier for use, but maybe you don't care about that for your use-case. I was considering trying Firebase as an intermediate solution, but haven't gotten around to it yet.\n\nGiven all these concerns, I haven't used Popylar for anything myself and it remains a work of conceptual art :-/\n\nI do know that some other people have been considering using it. As I recall, @peircej showed this to someone who then started using it, but I am fuzzy on the details of that.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"47c943b525bbb05887c8d1724f723c3ae15c6e40"},"timestamp":1549463264,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2MTA0MTgwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2906#issuecomment-461041800"},"message":"My method was to call a server with params (software version, platform, datetime) in the url, read them with PHP and store them with SQL. I used IP address to detect unique \"users\" (since GDPR I use a SHA of the IP). It's very simple to set up with a standard server setup, but it doesn't have the features of google analytics (e.g. geography mapping) or probably the resilience (we once lost several weeks of data when a database failed).\n\nI like the concept of GA and Popylar for better graphing, richer analysis and being more robust but I found that popylar didn't work quite as easily as I wanted. Mostly I think this is just that the google API call is poorly documented and I couldn't work out what parameters were valid combinations. In particular if I want to store the software version and the operating system then I couldn't use multiple parameters in a single call. You would have to create an \"event\" called OS and another \"event\" called version etc. Not as easy as using GA for regular website visits. It all just felt a bit clunky. I tried to get some of the info uploaded using an agent info string but couldn't make GA use that either. \n\nAs to concerns about privacy, note that GA provides the anonymous version and the non-anon version. If you turn off all the web marketing options then it is actually anonymous (can't be combined with the rest of google's data about the user). It's not anonymous when you add persistent tracking that (remarketing and advertising) and then you're legally bound by GDPR, assuming you have EU users. See https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/2700409","files":null}]}